{"ts":"2026-04-20T11:38:08Z","event":"clarify_critic","feature":"surface-weight-flow-g-s-in-transformedsample-flowsummary","findings":["Intent clarity HIGH bundles a mechanical transformer surfacing with a /diagnose divergence-interpretation change whose threshold is 'to be established during implementation' and references two alternative source docs — that ambiguity glosses over a real interpretive layer.","Scope boundedness HIGH is asserted from five AC bullets but silent on: callers of TransformedSample/FlowSummary beyond /diagnose, edge cases (all-zero weight flow, missing vf, pre- vs 1.8.0 fixtures), and the output format/placement of the /diagnose divergence line.","AC(c) outsources the threshold to 'DR-4 follow-up or EXTRACTION_SCIENCE_REFERENCE.md' without confirming either contains it; 'to be established during implementation' is definitionally leaving judgment to the implementer.","Requirements alignment marked N/A on the directory-existence technicality ignores de facto requirements in CLAUDE.md (BT-scale weight-artifact guidance, firmware 1.8.0 semantic/retention traps) that are directly relevant to time_to_first_nonzero_weight_flow_s and the divergence diagnostic.","Complexity 'simple' understates scope: the three-file estimate excludes docstring, 016 fixture golden-value regeneration for three new fields, /diagnose skill prose, and any knowledge-file edit; time_to_first_nonzero_weight_flow_s has no direct pump-flow analogue and needs a BT-noise-aware definition of 'nonzero'.","Criticality 'medium' understates the user-visible surface: /diagnose feeds user-facing channeling diagnoses (CLAUDE.md Core Rule: sour AND bitter = channeling, fix puck prep NOT grind); a miscalibrated divergence threshold could produce false channeling calls that mislead the user. Per clarify.md §5 default, skill/agentic-layer changes default to high.","The Supersedes clause about ticket 017's docs bullet is taken at face value without verifying ticket 017's content — gap-filling the clarify is supposed to surface."],"dispositions":{"apply":3,"dismiss":3,"ask":1},"applied_fixes":["Revised Requirements alignment from N/A to Partial: CLAUDE.md Core Rules document BT-scale weight artifacts (spikes, drops to 0g, null readings) that time_to_first_nonzero_weight_flow_s must handle defensively; firmware 1.8.0 retention/semantic-flip notes are tangentially relevant if fixtures span firmware versions; no strict conflicts.","Revised Complexity from simple to complex: modifies shared analysis infrastructure (transformers/shot.py consumed by /diagnose and /feedback); introduces time_to_first_nonzero_weight_flow_s with BT-noise-aware 'nonzero' definition required; affects user-facing diagnostic output; fixture-golden regeneration across 016's fixtures is non-trivial.","Revised Criticality from medium to high: /diagnose is a shared skill whose output feeds user-facing channeling diagnoses; a wrong or miscalibrated divergence threshold could drive incorrect fixes (grind vs puck prep); per clarify.md §5 default, skill/agentic-layer changes default to high."],"dismissals":[{"finding_index":1,"rationale":"Scope gaps identified (callers beyond /diagnose, edge-case handling, /diagnose output format) are appropriate subjects for Research (callers, fixture-version compatibility) and Spec (output format, edge-case handling). The ticket's five-bullet AC remains the scope anchor; these refinements occur downstream."},{"finding_index":2,"rationale":"The threshold discovery is the legitimate subject of Research. The ticket's 'to be established during implementation, not left to reviewer judgment' is a research charge with a clear fallback: Research will either locate a canonical threshold in DR-4 / EXTRACTION_SCIENCE_REFERENCE.md or propose one with rationale."},{"finding_index":6,"rationale":"Ticket 017 exists in the project and its /vf/ documentation bullet has been explicitly folded into this ticket's docstring-update AC. Verifying that the docstring update captures 017's intent belongs in Research review of the existing 017 content, not clarify."}],"status":"ok"}
